// Platform finance administration (DD-02 §3, ENV-06): the price book that
// admission freezes revisions from, the budget pools that fund operations
// and the tenant/project/operation actual-cost caps that admission checks.
//
// Every mutation is an operator command: it carries the command identity
// and the operator's verified user scope (P0.3), and Control decides on the
// verified roles, never on the caller's word. A price revision is
// immutable once published; withdrawing it stops new admission under it
// while prepared and in-flight dispatches keep settling under it. Lowering
// a pool or cap fences new admission only; it never revokes an issued
// permission or erases incurred cost.

